+# Independent official protocol-library peer (test-only)
+
+This adapter constructs the **unmodified** exported `sing-quic` TUIC/Hysteria2
+clients and servers selected by official sing-box **1.14.4**. It does not construct
+the sing-box CLI or NetworkManager. A library pass is **not** a full-program CLI
+pass. No Go/reference dependency is linked into or required by the product core.
+
+All protocol authentication, QUIC/TLS, HTTP/3 and UDP fragment processing is upstream
+code. This harness supplies only standard TLS configuration, a loopback-only dialer,
+a loopback-only ordinary payload relay, and destination-side assertions.
+
+## Source integrity
+
+Pinned to the official release [go.mod](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SagerNet/sing-box/v1.14.4/go.mod)
+and [go.sum](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/SagerNet/sing-box/v1.14.4/go.sum):
+
+- `github.com/sagernet/sing-quic v0.7.2-0.20261020082049-7e0a5869a5f4`
+- `github.com/sagernet/quic-go v0.61.0-sing-box-mod.12`
+- `github.com/sagernet/sing v0.9.7-0.20261023115459-5dc452e537bf`
+
+Both module and go.mod `h1` checksums for all three match the official release
+manifest. The checked-in `go.sum` locks the complete harness dependency graph.
+Never disable `GOSUMDB` verification; run `go mod verify` before building.
+The official release go.sum SHA-256 used for comparison is
+`a93ea3b691cdfbba29d49ac63ed8352601306d89625e0abc87e41241434e8592`.
+
+Validated compiler: official Go **1.26.10**, linux-amd64 archive SHA-256
+`ccfe7ae822d2c2f41f4fe7c956199967a4dac22d0ee0d2b2bfdb440aab3b20c5`,
+verified against `https://go.dev/dl/?mode=json&include=all` before extraction.
+The toolchain is test-only; it is not a new product dependency.
+
+## Reproduce
+
+Use an authorized, checksum-verified official Go compiler, with writable private
+`GOMODCACHE`/`GOCACHE`. From this directory:
+
+```sh
+export GOTOOLCHAIN=local GOPROXY=https://proxy.golang.org GOSUMDB=sum.golang.org
+go mod download
+go mod verify
+go vet ./...
+go build -mod=readonly -trimpath -buildvcs=false -o /absolute/test-output/reference-quic .
+```
+
+From the vp_core workspace (Rust 1.88.0 and unchanged Cargo.lock):
+
+```sh
+export CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0
+export VP_QUIC_REFERENCE=/absolute/test-output/reference-quic
+cargo test --locked -p vp-protocol --test quic_library_interop -- --include-ignored --nocapture
+cargo test --locked -p vp-protocol --test quic_auth_negative
+```
+
+The Rust tests supply fresh credentials, CA, signed leaf and private key over stdin;
+no keys are saved. Client and server listeners/targets are ephemeral loopback-only.
+The reverse client uses an owned per-instance CA store and normal certificate,
+signature and SNI validation. Wrong CA, wrong name and untrusted-default-root cases
+must produce actual TLS verification errors **and** no TCP/UDP destination traffic.
+Empty custom trust stores and insecure/custom-trust conflicts are rejected.
+No global trust store, route/firewall/TUN/system proxy, monitor or installer changes.
+
+## Coverage and limits
+
+Both directions: official library client -> vp_core inbound; vp_core outbound ->
+official library server. TUIC native-datagram and QUIC-stream modes; Hysteria2;
+authenticated TCP echo; reverse TCP half-close; UDP alternating two destinations,
+stable association source, payload/source validation and fragmentation. Wrong
+credentials cover TCP/UDP in both directions and both TUIC UDP modes.
+
+UDP payloads: TUIC **73 and 6000 bytes**; Hysteria2 **73 and 4096 bytes**.
+The unmodified official Hy2 peer declares `MaxUDPSize = 4096` and rejects larger
+writes locally. A first 6000-byte attempt failed before sending with
+`DATAGRAM frame too large (maximum: 4096 bytes)`; this is a reference-library limit,
+not a measured product wire failure or an implicit passed test.
+
+Full official CLI testing remains independently blocked before listening by sandbox
+netlink-monitor `EPERM`. These local library tests do not certify full CLI startup,
+non-loopback operation, native platforms, performance, optional obfuscation,
+all TLS policy combinations or complete protocol conformance.
